.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt GETTY 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm getty
.Nd set up a terminal and ask for a login name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar type Op Ar tty
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
program is run by
.Xr init 8
for each terminal marked
.Dq on
in
.Xr ttys 5 .
It opens
.Pa /dev/ Ns Ar tty
as the controlling terminal of a new session and as its standard input,
output and error, configures the line from the
.Xr gettytab 5
record
.Ar type
(or
.Dq default ) ,
prints a banner and a login prompt, and runs
.Xr login 1
with the name that is typed.
A
.Ar tty
of
.Dq -
means the terminal
.Nm
was started on.
.Pp
The banner is the record's
.Cm if
file, or else its
.Cm im
string, and the prompt is its
.Cm lm
string.
In each, the escapes
.Ql %t
(the terminal),
.Ql %h
(the host name),
.Ql %s ,
.Ql %r ,
.Ql %v ,
.Ql %m
(the system's name, release, version and machine),
.Ql %d
(the date and time) and
.Ql %%
are replaced.
.Pp
An empty line prompts again.
A break (a line holding a NUL character) switches to the record named by
.Cm nx ,
for serial lines whose speed is found by trying each in turn.
With
.Cm to
set,
.Nm
exits if no name is typed within that many seconds, and
.Xr init 8
starts a new one.
A record with
.Cm al
logs its user in automatically.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/gettytab -compact
.It Pa /etc/gettytab
terminal descriptions
.It Pa /etc/ttys
the terminals
.Xr init 8
runs
.Nm
on
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr gettytab 5 ,
.Xr ttys 5 ,
.Xr init 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
program appeared in
.At v6 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
